{"1-8":{"people":[{"id":"solomon-h8010","name":"Solomon","kind":"person","brief":"King of Judah","count":6,"firstVerse":1},{"id":"heth-h2845","name":"Heth","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Canaan","count":1,"firstVerse":1},{"id":"pharaoh-h6547k","name":"Pharaoh","kind":"person","brief":"A Pharaoh","count":1,"firstVerse":1},{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":1,"firstVerse":2},{"id":"david-h1732","name":"David","kind":"person","brief":"King of Judah","count":2,"firstVerse":4}],"places":[{"id":"ammon-h5983","name":"Ammon","kind":"place","brief":"","count":3,"firstVerse":1},{"id":"moab-h4124g","name":"Moab","kind":"place","brief":"In Edom","count":2,"firstVerse":1},{"id":"sidon-h6721h","name":"Sidon","kind":"place","brief":"","count":2,"firstVerse":1},{"id":"edom-h0123g","name":"Edom","kind":"place","brief":"In Edom","count":1,"firstVerse":1},{"id":"jerusalem-h3389","name":"Jerusalem","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":7}],"words":[{"base":"H8010","lemma":"שְׁלֹמֹה","tr":"she·lo·moh","gloss":"Solomon","lang":"h","inPassage":6,"uses":293},{"base":"H8251","lemma":"שִׁקּוּץ","tr":"shiq·quts","gloss":"abomination","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":28},{"base":"H0310","lemma":"אַחַר","tr":"a·char","gloss":"after","lang":"h","inPassage":5,"uses":715},{"base":"H3824","lemma":"לֵבָב","tr":"le·vav","gloss":"heart","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":252},{"base":"H0802","lemma":"אִשָּׁה","tr":"ish·shah","gloss":"woman","lang":"h","inPassage":5,"uses":781},{"base":"H5186","lemma":"נָטָה","tr":"na·tah","gloss":"to stretch","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":214},{"base":"H6722","lemma":"צִידֹנִי","tr":"tsi·do·ni","gloss":"Sidonian","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":16},{"base":"H5984","lemma":"עַמּוֹנִי","tr":"am·mo·ni","gloss":"Meunite","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":21},{"base":"H5237","lemma":"נׇכְרִי","tr":"nokh·ri","gloss":"foreign","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":45},{"base":"H6253","lemma":"עַשְׁתֹּ֫רֶת","tr":"ash·to·ret","gloss":"Ashtoreth","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":3}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"EXO","chapter":34,"verse":16,"verseEnd":16,"votes":15,"source":"both","text":"And when you take some of their daughters as brides for your sons, their daughters will prostitute themselves to their gods and cause your sons to do the same.","from":2},{"book":"DEU","chapter":7,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":14,"source":"openbible","text":"Do not intermarry with them. Do not give your daughters to their sons or take their daughters for your sons,","from":2},{"book":"DEU","chapter":7,"verse":4,"verseEnd":4,"votes":14,"source":"openbible","text":"because they will turn your sons away from following Me to serve other gods. Then the anger of the LORD will burn against you, and He will swiftly destroy you.","from":2},{"book":"JOS","chapter":23,"verse":12,"verseEnd":12,"votes":8,"source":"openbible","text":"For if you turn away and cling to the rest of these nations that remain among you, and if you intermarry and associate with them,","from":2},{"book":"JOS","chapter":23,"verse":13,"verseEnd":13,"votes":8,"source":"openbible","text":"know for sure that the LORD your God will no longer drive out these nations before you. Instead, they will become for you a snare and a trap, a scourge in your sides and thorns in your eyes, until you perish from this good land that the LORD your God has given you.","from":2},{"book":"EXO","chapter":23,"verse":32,"verseEnd":32,"votes":7,"source":"openbible","text":"You shall make no covenant with them or with their gods.","from":2},{"book":"EXO","chapter":23,"verse":33,"verseEnd":33,"votes":7,"source":"openbible","text":"They must not remain in your land, lest they cause you to sin against Me. For if you serve their gods, it will surely be a snare to you.”","from":2},{"book":"NUM","chapter":25,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":7,"source":"openbible","text":"While Israel was staying in Shittim, the men began to indulge in sexual immorality with the daughters of Moab,","from":2}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"kings-prophets","title":"Kings, prophets and the house of David","people":2},{"id":"royal-line","title":"The royal line: Judah to David to Jesus","people":2}]},"9-13":{"people":[{"id":"solomon-h8010","name":"Solomon","kind":"person","brief":"King of Judah","count":2,"firstVerse":9},{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":1,"firstVerse":9},{"id":"david-h1732","name":"David","kind":"person","brief":"King of Judah","count":2,"firstVerse":12}],"places":[{"id":"jerusalem-h3389","name":"Jerusalem","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":13}],"words":[{"base":"H7167","lemma":"קָרַע","tr":"qa·ra","gloss":"to tear","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":63},{"base":"H4616","lemma":"מַ֫עַן","tr":"ma·an","gloss":"because","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":272},{"base":"H6680","lemma":"צָוָה","tr":"tsa·vah","gloss":"to command","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":494},{"base":"H4467","lemma":"מַמְלָכָה","tr":"mam·la·khah","gloss":"kingdom","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":117},{"base":"H8010","lemma":"שְׁלֹמֹה","tr":"she·lo·moh","gloss":"Solomon","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":293},{"base":"H8104","lemma":"שָׁמַר","tr":"sha·mar","gloss":"to keep: obey","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":469},{"base":"H5650","lemma":"עֶ֫בֶד","tr":"e·ved","gloss":"servant","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":800},{"base":"H0599","lemma":"אָנַף","tr":"a·naph","gloss":"be angry","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":14},{"base":"H5973","lemma":"עִם","tr":"im","gloss":"with","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":1051},{"base":"H1732","lemma":"דָּוִד","tr":"da·vid","gloss":"David","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":1075}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"1KI","chapter":3,"verse":5,"verseEnd":5,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"One night at Gibeon the LORD appeared to Solomon in a dream, and God said, “Ask, and I will give it to you!”","from":9},{"book":"1KI","chapter":9,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"the LORD appeared to him a second time, as He had appeared to him at Gibeon.","from":9},{"book":"1KI","chapter":12,"verse":20,"verseEnd":20,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"When all Israel heard that Jeroboam had returned, they summoned him to the assembly and made him king over all Israel. Only the tribe of Judah followed the house of David.","from":13},{"book":"DEU","chapter":12,"verse":11,"verseEnd":11,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"then the LORD your God will choose a dwelling for His Name. And there you are to bring everything I command you: your burnt offerings and sacrifices, your tithes and special gifts, and all the choice offerings you vow to the LORD.","from":13},{"book":"1KI","chapter":11,"verse":31,"verseEnd":31,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"and said to Jeroboam, “Take ten pieces for yourself, for this is what the LORD, the God of Israel, says: ‘Behold, I will tear the kingdom out of the hand of Solomon, and I will give you ten tribes.","from":11},{"book":"1KI","chapter":11,"verse":32,"verseEnd":32,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"But one tribe will remain for the sake of My servant David and for the sake of Jerusalem, the city I have chosen out of all the tribes of Israel.","from":13},{"book":"1KI","chapter":12,"verse":15,"verseEnd":15,"votes":5,"source":"openbible","text":"So the king did not listen to the people, and indeed this turn of events was from the LORD, to fulfill the word He had spoken to Jeroboam son of Nebat through Ahijah the Shilonite.","from":11},{"book":"1KI","chapter":12,"verse":16,"verseEnd":16,"votes":5,"source":"openbible","text":"When all Israel saw that the king had refused to listen to them, they answered the king: “What portion do we have in David, and what inheritance in the son of Jesse? To your tents, O Israel! Look now to your own house, O David!” So the Israelites went home,","from":11}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"kings-prophets","title":"Kings, prophets and the house of David","people":2},{"id":"royal-line","title":"The royal line: Judah to David to Jesus","people":2}]},"14-25":{"people":[{"id":"hadad-h1908i","name":"Hadad","kind":"person","brief":"Father of Genubath","count":5,"firstVerse":14},{"id":"solomon-h8010","name":"Solomon","kind":"person","brief":"King of Judah","count":2,"firstVerse":14},{"id":"david-h1732","name":"David","kind":"person","brief":"King of Judah","count":3,"firstVerse":15},{"id":"joab-h3097g","name":"Joab","kind":"person","brief":"David's compatriot","count":3,"firstVerse":15},{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":2,"firstVerse":16},{"id":"pharaoh-h6547k","name":"Pharaoh","kind":"person","brief":"A Pharaoh","count":5,"firstVerse":18},{"id":"tahpenes-h8472g","name":"Tahpenes","kind":"person","brief":"Egyptian woman","count":2,"firstVerse":19},{"id":"father-of-tahpenes-h8472h","name":"father of Tahpenes","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":19},{"id":"sister-of-tahpenes-h8472i","name":"sister of Tahpenes","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":19},{"id":"genubath-h1592","name":"Genubath","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Hadad","count":1,"firstVerse":20},{"id":"eliada-h0450h","name":"Eliada","kind":"person","brief":"Father of Rezon","count":1,"firstVerse":23},{"id":"hadadezer-h1909","name":"Hadadezer","kind":"person","brief":"King of Zobah","count":1,"firstVerse":23},{"id":"rezon-h7331","name":"Rezon","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Eliada","count":1,"firstVerse":23}],"places":[{"id":"edom-h0123g","name":"Edom","kind":"place","brief":"In Edom","count":4,"firstVerse":14},{"id":"egypt-h4714g","name":"Egypt","kind":"place","brief":"","count":3,"firstVerse":17},{"id":"midian-h4080h","name":"Midian","kind":"place","brief":"In Edom","count":1,"firstVerse":18},{"id":"paran-h6290g","name":"Paran","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":18},{"id":"zobah-h6678g","name":"Zobah","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":23},{"id":"damascus-h1834","name":"Damascus","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":24},{"id":"syria-h0758i","name":"Syria","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":25}],"words":[{"base":"H1908","lemma":"הֲדַד","tr":"ha·dad","gloss":"Hadad","lang":"h","inPassage":6,"uses":12},{"base":"H6547","lemma":"פַּרְעֹה","tr":"par·oh","gloss":"Pharaoh","lang":"h","inPassage":7,"uses":274},{"base":"H8472","lemma":"תַּחְפְּנֵיס","tr":"tach·pe·nes","gloss":"Tahpenes","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":3},{"base":"H0123","lemma":"אֱדוֹם","tr":"e·dom","gloss":"Edom","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":100},{"base":"H7854","lemma":"שָׂטָן","tr":"sa·tan","gloss":"Satan","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":27},{"base":"H1592","lemma":"גְּנֻבַת","tr":"ge·nu·vat","gloss":"Genubath","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":2},{"base":"H0269","lemma":"אָחוֹת","tr":"a·chot","gloss":"sister","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":114},{"base":"H4714","lemma":"מִצְרַ֫יִם","tr":"mits·ra·yim","gloss":"Egypt","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":641},{"base":"H3097","lemma":"יוֹאָב","tr":"yo·av","gloss":"Joab","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":145},{"base":"H6290","lemma":"פָּארָן","tr":"pa·ran","gloss":"Paran","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":11}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"2SA","chapter":8,"verse":14,"verseEnd":14,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"He placed garrisons throughout Edom, and all the Edomites were subject to David. So the LORD made David victorious wherever he went.","from":15},{"book":"1CH","chapter":18,"verse":12,"verseEnd":12,"votes":6,"source":"openbible","text":"Moreover, Abishai son of Zeruiah struck down eighteen thousand Edomites in the Valley of Salt.","from":15},{"book":"1CH","chapter":18,"verse":13,"verseEnd":13,"votes":6,"source":"openbible","text":"He placed garrisons in Edom, and all the Edomites were subject to David. So the LORD made David victorious wherever he went.","from":15},{"book":"NUM","chapter":10,"verse":12,"verseEnd":12,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"and the Israelites set out from the Wilderness of Sinai, traveling from place to place until the cloud settled in the Wilderness of Paran.","from":18},{"book":"GEN","chapter":14,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"and the Horites in the area of Mount Seir, as far as El-paran, which is near the desert.","from":18},{"book":"GEN","chapter":14,"verse":15,"verseEnd":15,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"During the night, Abram divided his forces and routed Chedorlaomerʼs army, pursuing them as far as Hobah, north of Damascus.","from":24},{"book":"GEN","chapter":21,"verse":7,"verseEnd":7,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"She added, “Who would have told Abraham that Sarah would nurse children? Yet I have borne him a son in his old age.”","from":20},{"book":"GEN","chapter":21,"verse":21,"verseEnd":21,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"And while he was dwelling in the Wilderness of Paran, his mother got a wife for him from the land of Egypt.","from":18}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"kings-prophets","title":"Kings, prophets and the house of David","people":3},{"id":"royal-line","title":"The royal line: Judah to David to Jesus","people":2}]},"26-40":{"people":[{"id":"jeroboam-h3379g","name":"Jeroboam","kind":"person","brief":"King of N. Israel","count":5,"firstVerse":26},{"id":"solomon-h8010","name":"Solomon","kind":"person","brief":"King of Judah","count":5,"firstVerse":26},{"id":"ephraim-h0669g","name":"Ephraim","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Joseph","count":1,"firstVerse":26},{"id":"nebat-h5028","name":"Nebat","kind":"person","brief":"Father of Jeroboam","count":1,"firstVerse":26},{"id":"zeruah-h6871","name":"Zeruah","kind":"person","brief":"Jeroboam's mother","count":1,"firstVerse":26},{"id":"david-h1732","name":"David","kind":"person","brief":"King of Judah","count":7,"firstVerse":27},{"id":"joseph-h3130g","name":"Joseph","kind":"person","brief":"Jacob's son","count":1,"firstVerse":28},{"id":"ahijah-h0281h","name":"Ahijah","kind":"person","brief":"A prophet","count":2,"firstVerse":29},{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":4,"firstVerse":31},{"id":"shishak-h7895","name":"Shishak","kind":"person","brief":"A Pharaoh","count":1,"firstVerse":40}],"places":[{"id":"zeredah-h6868g","name":"Zeredah","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":26},{"id":"millo-h4407","name":"Millo","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":27},{"id":"jerusalem-h3389","name":"Jerusalem","kind":"place","brief":"","count":3,"firstVerse":29},{"id":"shiloh-h7887","name":"Shiloh","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":29},{"id":"ammon-h5983","name":"Ammon","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":33},{"id":"moab-h4124g","name":"Moab","kind":"place","brief":"In Edom","count":1,"firstVerse":33},{"id":"sidon-h6721h","name":"Sidon","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":33},{"id":"egypt-h4714g","name":"Egypt","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":40}],"words":[{"base":"H3379","lemma":"יָֽרָבְעָם","tr":"ya·rov·am","gloss":"Jeroboam","lang":"h","inPassage":6,"uses":104},{"base":"H1732","lemma":"דָּוִד","tr":"da·vid","gloss":"David","lang":"h","inPassage":8,"uses":1075},{"base":"H8010","lemma":"שְׁלֹמֹה","tr":"she·lo·moh","gloss":"Solomon","lang":"h","inPassage":6,"uses":293},{"base":"H7626","lemma":"שֵׁ֫בֶט","tr":"she·vet","gloss":"tribe: staff","lang":"h","inPassage":5,"uses":190},{"base":"H4616","lemma":"מַ֫עַן","tr":"ma·an","gloss":"because","lang":"h","inPassage":5,"uses":272},{"base":"H9031","lemma":"ךָּ","tr":"ka","gloss":"you","lang":"h","inPassage":5,"uses":727},{"base":"H5650","lemma":"עֶ֫בֶד","tr":"e·ved","gloss":"servant","lang":"h","inPassage":5,"uses":800},{"base":"H7168","lemma":"קֶ֫רַע","tr":"qe·ra","gloss":"rags","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":4},{"base":"H2708","lemma":"חֻקָּה","tr":"chuq·qah","gloss":"statute","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":104},{"base":"H0977","lemma":"בָּחַר","tr":"ba·char","gloss":"to choose","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":171}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"2SA","chapter":7,"verse":11,"verseEnd":11,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"and have done since the day I appointed judges over My people Israel. I will give you rest from all your enemies. The LORD declares to you that He Himself will establish a house for you.","from":38},{"book":"JOS","chapter":1,"verse":5,"verseEnd":5,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"No one shall stand against you all the days of your life. As I was with Moses, so will I be with you; I will never leave you nor forsake you.","from":38},{"book":"1KI","chapter":9,"verse":24,"verseEnd":24,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"As soon as Pharaohʼs daughter had come up from the City of David to the palace that Solomon had built for her, he built the supporting terraces.","from":27},{"book":"1KI","chapter":11,"verse":13,"verseEnd":13,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Yet I will not tear the whole kingdom away from him. I will give one tribe to your son for the sake of My servant David and for the sake of Jerusalem, which I have chosen.”","from":36},{"book":"1KI","chapter":12,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"When Jeroboam son of Nebat heard about this, he was still in Egypt where he had fled from King Solomon and had been living ever since.","from":26},{"book":"1KI","chapter":12,"verse":15,"verseEnd":15,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"So the king did not listen to the people, and indeed this turn of events was from the LORD, to fulfill the word He had spoken to Jeroboam son of Nebat through Ahijah the Shilonite.","from":29},{"book":"1KI","chapter":14,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"and Jeroboam said to his wife, “Now get up, disguise yourself so they will not recognize you as my wife, and go to Shiloh. For Ahijah the prophet is there; it was he who spoke about my kingship over this people.","from":29},{"book":"1KI","chapter":15,"verse":4,"verseEnd":4,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Nevertheless, for the sake of David, the LORD his God gave him a lamp in Jerusalem by raising up a son to succeed him and to make Jerusalem strong.","from":36}],"notes":[{"id":"1-sam-15-kingdom-torn","title":"The kingdom torn from Saul and from Solomon","kind":"prophecy"}],"groups":[{"id":"kings-prophets","title":"Kings, prophets and the house of David","people":5},{"id":"royal-line","title":"The royal line: Judah to David to Jesus","people":2},{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":2}]},"41-43":{"people":[{"id":"solomon-h8010","name":"Solomon","kind":"person","brief":"King of Judah","count":3,"firstVerse":41},{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":1,"firstVerse":42},{"id":"david-h1732","name":"David","kind":"person","brief":"King of Judah","count":1,"firstVerse":43},{"id":"rehoboam-h7346","name":"Rehoboam","kind":"person","brief":"King of Judah","count":1,"firstVerse":43}],"places":[{"id":"jerusalem-h3389","name":"Jerusalem","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":42}],"words":[{"base":"H8010","lemma":"שְׁלֹמֹה","tr":"she·lo·moh","gloss":"Solomon","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":293},{"base":"H4427","lemma":"מָלַךְ","tr":"ma·lakh","gloss":"to reign","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":348},{"base":"H7346","lemma":"רְחַבְעָם","tr":"re·chav·am","gloss":"Rehoboam","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":50},{"base":"H3499","lemma":"יֶ֫תֶר","tr":"ye·ter","gloss":"remainder","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":101},{"base":"H6912","lemma":"קָבַר","tr":"qa·var","gloss":"to bury","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":133},{"base":"H0705","lemma":"אַרְבָּעִים","tr":"ar·ba·im","gloss":"forty","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":135},{"base":"H2451","lemma":"חׇכְמָה","tr":"chokh·mah","gloss":"wisdom","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":153},{"base":"H5612","lemma":"סֵ֫פֶר","tr":"se·pher","gloss":"scroll: document","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":186},{"base":"H7901","lemma":"שָׁכַב","tr":"sha·khav","gloss":"to lie down: lay down","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":212},{"base":"H3789","lemma":"כָּתַב","tr":"ka·tav","gloss":"to write","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":224}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"1KI","chapter":2,"verse":10,"verseEnd":10,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Then David rested with his fathers and was buried in the City of David.","from":43},{"book":"2KI","chapter":21,"verse":18,"verseEnd":18,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"And Manasseh rested with his fathers and was buried in his palace garden, the garden of Uzza. And his son Amon reigned in his place.","from":43},{"book":"DEU","chapter":31,"verse":16,"verseEnd":16,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"And the LORD said to Moses, “You will soon rest with your fathers, and these people will rise up and prostitute themselves with the foreign gods of the land they are entering. They will forsake Me and break the covenant I have made with them.","from":43},{"book":"1KI","chapter":1,"verse":21,"verseEnd":21,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Otherwise, when my lord the king rests with his fathers, I and my son Solomon will be counted as criminals.”","from":43},{"book":"1KI","chapter":2,"verse":11,"verseEnd":11,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"The length of Davidʼs reign over Israel was forty years—seven years in Hebron and thirty-three years in Jerusalem.","from":42},{"book":"1KI","chapter":14,"verse":20,"verseEnd":20,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"And the length of Jeroboamʼs reign was twenty-two years, and he rested with his fathers, and his son Nadab reigned in his place.","from":43},{"book":"1KI","chapter":14,"verse":31,"verseEnd":31,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"And Rehoboam rested with his fathers and was buried with them in the City of David; his motherʼs name was Naamah the Ammonite. And his son Abijam reigned in his place.","from":43},{"book":"1KI","chapter":15,"verse":8,"verseEnd":8,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"And Abijam rested with his fathers and was buried in the City of David, and his son Asa reigned in his place.","from":43}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"kings-prophets","title":"Kings, prophets and the house of David","people":3},{"id":"royal-line","title":"The royal line: Judah to David to Jesus","people":3}]}}